isible gear he's  using an invisible Chatel so be careful  now Roy only shows up when you play in  offline mode and he can drop the items  you see on screen but the true value of  this NPC invasion comes when you're a  part of the champions covenant as you  might know when you kill an invader as a  part of the champions covenant you'll  get an or stone these can be traded in  at the victors stone for the rewards on  screen now these or stones take ages to  get and the biggest reward  actually requires 50 of them and 50  invasions will usually take a few  playthroughs to accrue since NPC red  phantoms don't usually respawn when you  rest at the bonfire but Roy is different  he'll respawn 12 times after resting at  the bonfire just go down and up this  ladder and you trigger his arrival then  kill him rested the bonfire repeat this  12 times then use a bonfire aesthetic to  reset his respawn this is by far the  fastest way to get all the all stones  required for the victors covenant to  play Dark Souls to offline  if you're wondering sign out of your  account on your console or start steam  in offline mode thing you missed number  4 there are red phantoms exclusive to  New Game+ down the pit and they appear  at the bottom of the drop after the  exploding mummies so one of these drops  the dingy set which is exclusive to New  Game+ and it resembles the firekeepers  dingy set from Dark Souls 1 down to the  last detail even the skirt is  blood-stained so does this mean that  this red phantom is anastasiya there are  a lot of links and callbacks to Dark  Souls 1 but this is just one of those  links that really confuses me from a  lore perspective number 5 so we talked  about how from had a Heineken beer can  in one of their textures well they've  done it again look closely in one of  these pillars of trash and you will see  a car wheel I know time is convoluted  but this [ __ ] is too much number 6 now  we get to some of my favorite ones you  know that heartbeat you hear 